  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (173 tests, 0 failed).\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):** I added `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release`. `removeItem` now throws `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` if you try to remove more than is available. Expiry uses only the store's `clock`, and a reservation counts as expired once `clock() >= creation time + ttlMs`. `confirm` returns `{sku, stock}`, which the API uses for its response.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`. I added `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id`, with the status codes you listed.\n- **Tests (`test/reservations.test.js`):** The new tests cover the store behaviour, the API flow, the exact expiry boundary and idempotent release.\n\n- **`ttlMs` not validated:** I didn't validate `ttlMs`, since the spec doesn't say what to do with a bad value. A missing or non-numeric `ttlMs` makes the reservation expire immediately.\n- **Other `POST /reservations` errors:** Any error from `POST /reservations` other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400.",
